and then swapping out the hood ornament

00:35:41.600 --> 00:35:43.600
for a BMW logo

00:35:43.600 --> 00:35:45.600
you might fool people

00:35:45.600 --> 00:35:47.600
like me who don't know their cars

00:35:47.600 --> 00:35:49.600
but a knowledgeable person is

00:35:49.600 --> 00:35:51.600
definitely going to see through that

00:35:51.600 --> 00:35:53.600
no no no what's much harder

00:35:53.600 --> 00:35:55.600
is to have a clunker

00:35:55.600 --> 00:35:57.600
and then go through the painstaking

00:35:57.600 --> 00:35:59.600
process of rebuilding

00:35:59.600 --> 00:36:01.600
the engine

00:36:01.600 --> 00:36:03.600
and that's what true Christian spirituality

00:36:03.600 --> 00:36:05.600
is all about Christ is not

00:36:05.600 --> 00:36:07.600
interested in you and I slapping

00:36:07.600 --> 00:36:09.600
a Jesus hood ornament on the

00:36:09.600 --> 00:36:11.600
car of our metaphorical

00:36:11.600 --> 00:36:13.600
life he's interested

00:36:13.600 --> 00:36:15.600
in rebuilding the engine

00:36:15.600 --> 00:36:17.600
you say what do you mean by the

00:36:17.600 --> 00:36:19.600
engine I mean the inside of us

00:36:19.600 --> 00:36:21.600
our motivations our

00:36:21.600 --> 00:36:23.600
values our desires

00:36:23.600 --> 00:36:25.600
our loves who we love

00:36:25.600 --> 00:36:27.600
how we love he did not come

00:36:27.600 --> 00:36:29.600
to give us cosmetic surgery

00:36:29.600 --> 00:36:31.600
to pretty us up on the

00:36:31.600 --> 00:36:33.600
outside he came as the great physician

00:36:33.600 --> 00:36:35.600
offering all

00:36:35.600 --> 00:36:37.600
of humanity heart surgery

00:36:37.600 --> 00:36:39.600
surgery soul

00:36:39.600 --> 00:36:41.600
surgery this is what being

00:36:41.600 --> 00:36:43.600
a Christian is it's signing up for the

00:36:43.600 --> 00:36:45.600
difficult process of having

00:36:45.600 --> 00:36:47.600
our absolute obsession

00:36:47.600 --> 00:36:49.600
with being externally

00:36:49.600 --> 00:36:51.600
bigger and better and

00:36:51.600 --> 00:36:53.600
greater and

00:36:53.600 --> 00:36:55.600
it's having all of that turned

00:36:55.600 --> 00:36:57.600
upside down

00:36:57.600 --> 00:36:59.600
or perhaps I should say inside

00:36:59.600 --> 00:37:01.600
out because we go

00:37:01.600 --> 00:37:03.600
from being obsessed

00:37:03.600 --> 00:37:05.600
with becoming better

00:37:05.600 --> 00:37:07.600
out there

00:37:07.600 --> 00:37:09.600
in this kind of in the outward

00:37:09.600 --> 00:37:11.600
appearances to slowly

00:37:11.600 --> 00:37:13.600
becoming obsessed

00:37:13.600 --> 00:37:15.600
with who we are becoming

00:37:15.600 --> 00:37:17.600
in here

00:37:17.600 --> 00:37:19.600
the way

00:37:19.600 --> 00:37:21.600
that Jesus put it once

00:37:21.600 --> 00:37:23.600
he said this what good is it

00:37:23.600 --> 00:37:25.600
if you gain the whole world

00:37:25.600 --> 00:37:27.600
but lose your

00:37:27.600 --> 00:37:29.600
soul

00:37:29.600 --> 00:37:31.600
that's what Jesus is all about

00:37:31.600 --> 00:37:33.600
not who you are on the outside

00:37:33.600 --> 00:37:35.600
remember we look at the outward

00:37:35.600 --> 00:37:37.600
appearance where does God look

00:37:37.600 --> 00:37:39.600
at the heart so his question

00:37:39.600 --> 00:37:41.600
is who are you becoming

00:37:41.600 --> 00:37:43.600
on the inside

00:37:43.600 --> 00:37:45.600
are you more patient

00:37:45.600 --> 00:37:47.600
than you were a year ago

00:37:47.600 --> 00:37:49.600
are you more honest

00:37:49.600 --> 00:37:51.600
more courageous

00:37:51.600 --> 00:37:53.600
more kind

00:37:53.600 --> 00:37:55.600
I listened to an interview recently

00:37:55.600 --> 00:37:57.600
with Dr. Jim

00:37:57.600 --> 00:37:59.600
Layer he is a performance

00:37:59.600 --> 00:38:01.600
psychologist who has worked with hundreds

00:38:01.600 --> 00:38:03.600
of the best just the best athletes

00:38:03.600 --> 00:38:05.600
in the world across like a variety

00:38:05.600 --> 00:38:07.600
of sports from tennis

00:38:07.600 --> 00:38:09.600
basketball golf to even Olympians

00:38:09.600 --> 00:38:11.600
and not only

00:38:11.600 --> 00:38:13.600
has he worked with like people in these domains

00:38:13.600 --> 00:38:15.600
but he's worked with like the

00:38:15.600 --> 00:38:17.600
best of the best we're talking like

00:38:17.600 --> 00:38:19.600
Olympic gold medalists

00:38:19.600 --> 00:38:21.600
even in tennis

00:38:21.600 --> 00:38:23.600
he's worked with Roger Federer and

00:38:23.600 --> 00:38:25.600
Monica Sellis who both have been number

00:38:25.600 --> 00:38:27.600
one in their respective

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:29.600
kind of

00:38:29.600 --> 00:38:31.600
in tennis

00:38:31.600 --> 00:38:33.600
these are like big people big names

00:38:33.600 --> 00:38:35.600
but he noticed a trend

00:38:35.600 --> 00:38:37.600
and he described it

00:38:37.600 --> 00:38:39.600
this way he said that he worked with people

00:38:39.600 --> 00:38:41.600
who reached the top of their field

00:38:41.600 --> 00:38:43.600
and they would have

00:38:43.600 --> 00:38:45.600
conversations with him

00:38:45.600 --> 00:38:47.600
after they won the big match

00:38:47.600 --> 00:38:49.600
of the game and now they were

00:38:49.600 --> 00:38:51.600
you know Super Bowl champion

00:38:51.600 --> 00:38:53.600
or NBA champion or gold medalist

00:38:53.600 --> 00:38:55.600
and they would meet with him

00:38:55.600 --> 00:38:57.600
because he was their performance

00:38:57.600 --> 00:38:59.600
psychologist and they would meet with him

00:38:59.600 --> 00:39:01.600
afterwards and they would

00:39:01.600 --> 00:39:03.600
say something like this

00:39:03.600 --> 00:39:05.600
I don't

00:39:05.600 --> 00:39:07.600
feel any different

00:39:07.600 --> 00:39:09.600
like

00:39:09.600 --> 00:39:11.600
I thought I would feel

00:39:11.600 --> 00:39:13.600
complete

00:39:13.600 --> 00:39:15.600
somehow at peace

00:39:15.600 --> 00:39:17.600
like this has been my dream for so long

00:39:17.600 --> 00:39:19.600
and now I'm here

00:39:19.600 --> 00:39:21.600
and it's all

00:39:21.600 --> 00:39:23.600
sort of empty

00:39:23.600 --> 00:39:25.600
but then

00:39:25.600 --> 00:39:27.600
Dr. Laird said he would talk with other people

00:39:27.600 --> 00:39:29.600
who also reached the top

00:39:29.600 --> 00:39:31.600
of their field but they were

00:39:31.600 --> 00:39:33.600
so happy

00:39:33.600 --> 00:39:35.600
but he noticed they were happy before

00:39:35.600 --> 00:39:37.600
they became number one

00:39:37.600 --> 00:39:39.600
or Olympic champion or whatever

00:39:39.600 --> 00:39:41.600
and so he became

00:39:41.600 --> 00:39:43.600
quite obsessed with

00:39:43.600 --> 00:39:45.600
figuring out

00:39:45.600 --> 00:39:47.600
well why on earth

00:39:47.600 --> 00:39:49.600
like how is it that people

00:39:49.600 --> 00:39:51.600
could end up in these

00:39:51.600 --> 00:39:53.600
two very different places

00:39:53.600 --> 00:39:55.600
and eventually he figured it

00:39:55.600 --> 00:39:57.600
out and this is what he said

00:39:57.600 --> 00:39:59.600
he said I came to understand

00:39:59.600 --> 00:40:01.600
that we all

00:40:01.600 --> 00:40:03.600
all human beings

00:40:03.600 --> 00:40:05.600
we all have two

00:40:05.600 --> 00:40:07.600
scorecards

00:40:07.600 --> 00:40:09.600
the first scorecard is about

00:40:09.600 --> 00:40:11.600
our outward success

00:40:11.600 --> 00:40:13.600
and

00:40:13.600 --> 00:40:15.600
that's where society tells us to focus

00:40:15.600 --> 00:40:17.600
but there

00:40:17.600 --> 00:40:19.600
is a second scorecard

00:40:19.600 --> 00:40:21.600
and it's

00:40:21.600 --> 00:40:23.600
actually the more important scorecard

00:40:23.600 --> 00:40:25.600
the second scorecard is an

00:40:25.600 --> 00:40:27.600
internal scorecard

00:40:27.600 --> 00:40:29.600
and it's about

00:40:29.600 --> 00:40:31.600
our character

00:40:31.600 --> 00:40:33.600
what kind of people

00:40:33.600 --> 00:40:35.600
are we becoming

00:40:35.600 --> 00:40:37.600
he said the first group

00:40:37.600 --> 00:40:39.600
the unhappy group

00:40:39.600 --> 00:40:41.600
they were more inclined he found

00:40:41.600 --> 00:40:43.600
to ignore

00:40:43.600 --> 00:40:45.600
or even sacrifice

00:40:45.600 --> 00:40:47.600
who they were from an integrity

00:40:47.600 --> 00:40:49.600
and character standpoint

00:40:49.600 --> 00:40:51.600
in order to make it

00:40:51.600 --> 00:40:53.600
to the top of the first scorecard

00:40:53.600 --> 00:40:55.600
in other words they were going to get

00:40:55.600 --> 00:40:57.600
to the top regardless of whether or not

00:40:57.600 --> 00:40:59.600
they had to lie, cheat, tear

00:40:59.600 --> 00:41:01.600
others down on their way up like whatever it took

00:41:01.600 --> 00:41:03.600
whereas the second group

00:41:03.600 --> 00:41:05.600
they had such joy

00:41:05.600 --> 00:41:07.600
because they were winning

00:41:07.600 --> 00:41:09.600
on their own

00:41:09.600 --> 00:41:11.600
internal character

00:41:11.600 --> 00:41:13.600
scorecard which meant

00:41:13.600 --> 00:41:15.600
they could be at peace

00:41:15.600 --> 00:41:17.600
with whatever happened externally

00:41:17.600 --> 00:41:19.600
and so I'm listening

00:41:19.600 --> 00:41:21.600
to this interview with Dr. Lair

00:41:21.600 --> 00:41:23.600
and I'm just thinking to myself

00:41:23.600 --> 00:41:25.600
my goodness this is what the bible has been

00:41:25.600 --> 00:41:27.600
naming I mean think back to our text

00:41:27.600 --> 00:41:29.600
man looks at

00:41:29.600 --> 00:41:31.600
scorecard number one

00:41:31.600 --> 00:41:33.600
the outward scorecard

00:41:33.600 --> 00:41:35.600
but God

00:41:35.600 --> 00:41:37.600
looks at the

00:41:37.600 --> 00:41:39.600
inner scorecard

00:41:39.600 --> 00:41:41.600
or think back to Jesus quote what good is it

00:41:41.600 --> 00:41:43.600
to climb to the tippy top

00:41:43.600 --> 00:41:45.600
of scorecard number one

00:41:45.600 --> 00:41:47.600
but to be the worst

00:41:47.600 --> 00:41:49.600
kind of failure

00:41:49.600 --> 00:41:51.600
at scorecard number

00:41:51.600 --> 00:41:53.600
two right gaining the

00:41:53.600 --> 00:41:55.600
whole world losing the

00:41:55.600 --> 00:41:57.600
soul you see the way of the world is

00:41:57.600 --> 00:41:59.600
an obsession with the first

00:41:59.600 --> 00:42:01.600
scorecard but the path

00:42:01.600 --> 00:42:03.600
of Christ

00:42:03.600 --> 00:42:05.600
it's a switch

00:42:05.600 --> 00:42:07.600
it is a new orientation

00:42:07.600 --> 00:42:09.600
towards the second

00:42:09.600 --> 00:42:11.600
scorecard

00:42:11.600 --> 00:42:13.600
it's a new orientation

00:42:13.600 --> 00:42:15.600
towards who we are becoming

00:42:15.600 --> 00:42:17.600
who we are becoming on the

00:42:17.600 --> 00:42:19.600
inside right

00:42:19.600 --> 00:42:21.600
our character our integrity

00:42:21.600 --> 00:42:23.600
our love it's what has been called

00:42:23.600 --> 00:42:25.600
down through the centuries

00:42:25.600 --> 00:42:27.600
our Christ

00:42:27.600 --> 00:42:29.600
likeness in other words

00:42:29.600 --> 00:42:31.600
how deeply we embody

00:42:31.600 --> 00:42:33.600
the radiant love

00:42:33.600 --> 00:42:35.600
of the God we've come to know

00:42:35.600 --> 00:42:37.600
in Jesus

00:42:37.600 --> 00:42:39.600
so am I saying that

00:42:39.600 --> 00:42:41.600
big things are bad

00:42:41.600 --> 00:42:43.600
that being an outward success is bad

00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:45.600
that scorecard number one is evil

00:42:45.600 --> 00:42:47.600
no no I'm not saying that

00:42:47.600 --> 00:42:49.600
in fact you may even find

00:42:49.600 --> 00:42:51.600
that getting your internal world

00:42:51.600 --> 00:42:53.600
properly oriented

00:42:53.600 --> 00:42:55.600
heck that might even help you externally

00:42:55.600 --> 00:42:57.600
so no I'm not

00:42:57.600 --> 00:42:59.600
saying that being a big person doing big things

00:42:59.600 --> 00:43:01.600
in big places or something

00:43:01.600 --> 00:43:03.600
that's somehow inherently bad

00:43:03.600 --> 00:43:05.600
what I'm saying is

00:43:05.600 --> 00:43:07.600
don't obsess

00:43:07.600 --> 00:43:09.600
there

00:43:09.600 --> 00:43:11.600
instead

00:43:11.600 --> 00:43:13.600
focus here

00:43:13.600 --> 00:43:15.600
focus on the second

00:43:15.600 --> 00:43:17.600
scorecard because when we

00:43:17.600 --> 00:43:19.600
embrace that switch

00:43:19.600 --> 00:43:21.600
then we can begin

00:43:21.600 --> 00:43:23.600
to embrace simply

00:43:23.600 --> 00:43:25.600
being

00:43:25.600 --> 00:43:27.600
us

00:43:27.600 --> 00:43:29.600
like that's

00:43:29.600 --> 00:43:31.600
that's the greatest thing to be

00:43:31.600 --> 00:43:33.600
ourselves

00:43:33.600 --> 00:43:35.600
isn't it amazing how we spend our

00:43:35.600 --> 00:43:37.600
whole lives trying

00:43:37.600 --> 00:43:39.600
to be comfortable

00:43:39.600 --> 00:43:41.600
being

00:43:41.600 --> 00:43:43.600
us

00:43:43.600 --> 00:43:45.600
and let's be honest

00:43:45.600 --> 00:43:47.600
most of us are

00:43:47.600 --> 00:43:49.600
pretty invisible

00:43:49.600 --> 00:43:51.600
like all things considered

00:43:51.600 --> 00:43:53.600
we're very tiny people in the world

00:43:53.600 --> 00:43:55.600
and most of us work

00:43:55.600 --> 00:43:57.600
